re (ℝ × ℝ). On ℝ×ℝ the predicate pi.map fst = mu ∧ pi.map snd = nu is exactly right. Fix: take {A B} measurable spaces with mu : Measure A, nu : Measure B and pi : Measure (A × B), keeping the same body."},{"obj_id":"ass:ot-formulation-support","verdict":"faithful-refinement","note":"Both pi0 and pi1 are required to be probability measures on the ambient ((ℝ × X) × ℝ) with no mass outside {u ∈ [0,1], y ∈ Yset}, and X is the carrier type of 𝒳. This is the standard ambient-plus-full-mass idiom for a probability measure on 𝒴×[0,1]×𝒳; the coordinate reordering ((u,x),y) only changes the representation. Imposing it for both w ∈ {0,1} follows pin-29."}],"substrate_gates":[],"escalate":{"kind":"scaffold-mismatch","obj_id":"ass:couplings-probability-measure","reason":"The carrier is typed only on Measure (ℝ × ℝ), but the frozen node is about a probability measure on a general product 𝒜×ℬ of measurable state spaces, which the generic IsCoupling already covers. Generalize CouplingIsProbability and CouplingMarginals (same bodies) to arbitrary measurable A, B.","unpinned":"","witness":null}}

