{"statement_verdicts":[{"obj_id":"def:ot-formulation","verdict":"matched","note":"ccotValueSet lists every value θ(π1)−θ(π0) reached by a feasible pair, so its least and greatest elements are the problem's min and max. thetaComp(π) = ∫ y·ω(x,u) dπ on ((u,x),y). IsFeasiblePair imposes all constraints for both w at once (pin-29). (i) Treated/UntreatedCompatible: for P_{Z,X}-a.e. (z,x) and every measurable A, ∫ over R_w(p(z,x)) of π_w(A|u,x) du = H_{w,x}(p(z,x),A), with R_1 = (0,p] and R_0 = (p,1] as in selRegion. Because the marginal is du⊗P_X, the choice of condKernel version only matters on a set of x of P_X-measure zero, so the constraint does not depend on the version. (ii) UniformCovariateMarginal: π_w.fst = Leb|(0,1) ⊗ P_X, which is the paper's du P_obs(dx). (iii) FeasibleSupport: π_w is a probability measure (already forced by (ii)) and gives zero mass outside u∈[0,1], y∈𝒴. This is support on 𝒴×[0,1]×𝒳, a conservative extension from the ambient ℝ×X×ℝ. H, P_{Z,X} and P_X are parameters of ObservedTransportData and are instantiated by transportData. Both directions hold."}],"assumption_verdicts":[{"obj_id":"ass:pin-24","verdict":"faithful-refinement","note":"l2Error is the eLpNorm of (fit n a c − truth c) in L2(xLaw M), i.e. over the marginal law of X with the fitted function (fixed a) and the component/instrument index c held fixed. squaredError is pinned to its square. NuisanceRates gives, for each c, ExtendedLittleOp: μ{ε·n^{-1/4} ≤ error} → 0 for every ε > 0, which is o_P(n^{-1/4}) over the sample-and-partition space A. Only even sample sizes 2(n+1) are indexed, which matches the paper's split into two halves of size n/2 each. The EqualHalfSplit conjunct writes out that sampling setup: a random disjoint pair of halves, independent of the observations. Its uniform-law clause is the I_1/I_2 symbol realization, which is judged in that symbol cluster. Both directions hold under the paper's procedure."},{"obj_id":"ass:pin-31","verdict":"faithful-refinement","note":"With 0-based indexing, liv k for k<K is L_{k+1} = [p̲_{k+1}, p̄_{k+1}]. gap k = (gapLo k, gapHi k) = (p̄_k, p̲_{k+1}) with p̄_0 = 0, for k = 0..K−1, i.e. G_k. tail = (p̄_K, 1], or (0,1] when K = 0. The extra ∩[0,1] on the gaps does not change [0,1] minus the union. volume(...) = 0 is exactly ∫ du = 0 over that set. Equivalent."},{"obj_id":"ass:pin-32","verdict":"faithful-refinement","note":"The statement is ∀ᵐ x ∂P_X of the pin-31 null-partition predicate for CondRangeDecomposition x = RangeDecomposition(range z ↦ p(z,x)), i.e. p(𝒵,x) as in def:range-decomposition-cov. Through pin-31 this covers L_k(x) for 1≤k≤K_x, G_k(x) for 0≤k<K_x and the tail (p̄_{K_x}(x),1], up to Lebesgue-null sets. Equivalent."},{"obj_id":"ass:pin-37","verdict":"faithful-refinement","note":"The nuisance list is fixed by the type NuisanceBin = NuisanceBinData, whose fields are: prop p(z,x); pLev, P1 and piLev on PositiveIndex K (k = 1..K, so there is no free p_0, P_{1,0} or π_0); tauLev and share a_{j,k}(z,x) on RegularIndex; gammaFull on k < K; gamma; and gammaTail γ_K. This matches the pinned η. The Prop records the structural zeros p_0 = P_{1,0} = 0 through positiveValue at 0, which is true by definition, just as the paper's convention is. Equivalent; under the binding ruling, admissibility (componentwise reading) is not re-raised."}],"substrate_gates":[],"escalate":null}

