{"statement_verdicts":[{"obj_id":"def:dml-level-recovery","verdict":"matched","note":"Checked recoverLevels → recoverLevelsAt, recoveryActive, recoveryEdge, recoveryComponent, componentAverage and recoveryComponents against the NL and pins 43, 3 and 4. Ŝ_0 = {z : p̄_2(z) ≤ ρ_n}, and only baseline vertices with p̄_2 > ρ_n stay active; every policy vertex stays. Two distinct active vertices are joined exactly when their values differ by less than gap/2, and components are taken under the reflexive-transitive closure (pin-3). Components are sorted by their average over all member vertices. Ŝ_k for k ≥ 1 is the k-th component containing a baseline vertex, and p̂_0 = 0. T̂_{j,k} for j ≥ 1 is the j-th policy-containing component whose average lies in [p̂_k, p̂_{k+1}) when k < K, or in [p̂_K, 1] when k = K (pin-43). T̂_{0,k} = ∅, which matches the core convention that T_{0,k} is empty and q_{0,k} = p_k is only a boundary. The threshold hypothesis RecoveryThresholdAdmissible is the pin-4 condition on ρ_n, and gap > 0 is c_gap. The pLev and qLev fields are scalar component averages; the fitted scores use the fitted nuisances, while L.pLev appears only in the population (true-nuisance) definitions. Remaining residual: ties between distinct components with equal averages are broken by Finset.toList order, and the NL does not say how to order ties either; this is a measure-zero edge case and not drift."},{"obj_id":"def:dml-estimation-procedure","verdict":"matched","note":"Unfolded DynamicContFit, EqualHalfSplit, ContinuousFitScope, DMLLearningSteps, recoveredData, pBar, fittedContScore and dmlRV. The random partition is a uniform equal-halves split that is independent of the data; this is the paper's own sampling node ass:dml-equal-split. Odd n is left unconstrained because n/2 presupposes even n. p̂ is the first-stage learner on I₁ clipped to [0,1], q̂ = policyProp φ p̂, and p̄_2, q̄_2 average over the I₂ covariates. Levels are recovered with ρ_n admissible and gap > 0. Nuisances are fit on I₁ given the recovered sets: p̂_k regresses W on Z ∈ Ŝ_k; π̂ and τ̂ are clipped to [cπ/2, 1]; γ̂_full = (clipped higherPolicy) − (clipped higherBaseline) via ContProbabilitiesClippedBeforeDifference; γ̂_{j,k} and γ̂_K are clipped to [0,1]; shares come from the simplex-valued multinomial learner; ν̂ is the moment regression clipped to [y_min, y_max]; M± are clipped to [0,1], J± to the band, and J_full± to [y_min, y_max]. Minus-side index types exclude k = 0. θ̂ is the I₂ average of the fitted orthogonal score. PolicyDifferentiable (equivalent to pin-17) and the measurability clauses are domain and regularity presuppositions of ∂φ/∂p and of the estimator being a random variable."},{"obj_id":"def:dml-continuous-outcome-algorithm","verdict":"matched","note":"Same body as IsDMLProcedure, so the same check applies step by step. Step 1 is the split; step 2 is the clipped p̂ and q̂ = φ(·, ·, p̂) on I₁; step 3 averages over I₂ covariates, assigns Ŝ_0 by the ρ_n threshold (pin-4), joins vertices closer than c_gap/2 and orders the components. The remaining I₁ fits, clips, simplex shares and quantile moment regression match the algorithm, and minus-side objects are omitted at k = 0. The output adds σ̂² = varianceRV = |I₂|⁻¹ Σ_{i∈I₂} (ψ̂(O_i) − θ̂)², where θ̂ is the same score average; this matches the algorithm's Return line."}],"assumption_verdicts":[{"obj_id":"ass:pin-4","verdict":"faithful-refinement","note":"S₀ n a = {z : pb n a z ≤ ρ_n}, and ρ is a deterministic ℕ → ℝ sequence that is Antitone, tends to 0, and has n^(1/4)·ρ_n → ∞ (real rpow). The extra clause ∀ n, 0 < ρ_n is entailed: Antitone plus the limit 0 gives ρ_n ≥ 0, and ρ_n = 0 at any n would force ρ ≡ 0 from then on, which contradicts the divergence. Both directions hold."},{"obj_id":"ass:pin-47","verdict":"faithful-refinement","note":"rearrangeP1 sets P̂*_{1,k}(x), for k ∈ 1..K, to entry k−1 of the nondecreasing mergeSort (· ≤ ·) of the clipped vector (min 1 (max 0 P̂_{1,i})(x))_{i=1..K}. The list