 is encoded as the conjunction of two implications, which is equivalent. (3) Conclusion. Sample size is N=2(n+1), so sqrt(n+1)=sqrt(N/2). The Lean gives Op(N^{-1/2}) consistency and convergence in law to N(0,σ²), where σ²=∫(ψ(O;η)−θ)² under the observation law. The sample variance over I2, centred at θ̂, converges in probability to σ². Everything the Lean adds is harmless. The free parameter `ch` is unused by both regimes. hSeparation is implied by hGapWitness. hSplit is repeated inside the fit scopes. x0 only indexes the population LevelStructure, which hOrder makes invariant in x. The theorem holds for every valid witness gap/cpi, which makes it stronger than the paper. Proofs may be sorry; they are not judged here."}],"assumption_verdicts":[],"substrate_gates":[],"escalate":null}

